      "hex": "#ef4444"
    },
    "orange": {
      "hex": "#f97316"
    },
    "gold": {
      "hex": "#f59e0b"
    },
    "green": {
      "hex": "#10b981"
    },
    "blue": {
      "hex": "#0ea5e9"
    }
  },
  "category": {
    "$comment": "Theme-stable categorical set for telling unrelated groups apart at a glance (marketplace app categories today) when there are more groups than --chart-1..5 covers. Not semantic — a category's hue carries no meaning beyond 'not the others'. Formalizes CI-Hub's onboarding CATEGORY_ACCENTS (packages/frontend/src/modules/onboarding/components/recommendations-step.tsx). Add new keys as new categories appear; never reuse a hue for two live categories, and never reuse a status or level hex (a finance chip must not read as a warning) — the contract test enforces both.",
